## 5. Essential Performance Optimizations (2025)

### S-Tier (Critical — Always Do)
| Optimization | Technique |
|-------------|-----------|
| **Use `requestAnimationFrame`** | Never `setInterval`/`setTimeout`. rAF synchronises with display refresh rate and pauses when the tab is hidden. |
| **Integer coordinates** | `Math.floor()` all draw coordinates. Sub-pixel rendering forces anti-aliasing recalculations. |
| **Pre-render to offscreen canvas** | Cache all static/complex drawings. Use `drawImage(cachedCanvas, x, y)` in the game loop. |
| **Avoid scaling in `drawImage`** | Pre-scale assets at load time and store in cache. Never scale during hot loop. |

### A-Tier (High Impact)
| Optimization | Technique |
|-------------|-----------|
| **Batch canvas calls** | Group `fillStyle`/`strokeStyle` changes — draw all red objects, then all blue objects. |
| **Minimise state changes** | `save()`/`restore()` have CPU cost. Manage state manually where possible. |
| **Partial clearRect** | Clear only the dirty regions, not the entire canvas. |
| **Avoid `shadowBlur`** | Extremely expensive. Pre-bake shadows into sprite sheets instead. |

### B-Tier (Good to Have)
| Optimization | Technique |
|-------------|-----------|
| **Texture atlases** | Combine all character sprites into one PNG to reduce GPU texture switches. |
| **Object pooling** | Reuse enemy/projectile objects instead of creating/destroying them each frame. |
| **Spatial partitioning** | Only collision-check objects in the same grid cell / quadtree region. |
| **Disable alpha if not needed** | `canvas.getContext('2d', { alpha: false })` — lets the browser skip compositing. |

